{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>And he said, הֲכִי קָרָא, etc.</b> Meaning: he expresses astonishment — ״הֲכִי קָרָא שְׁמוֹ יַעֲקֹב?״ (Did he really call his name Jacob?) And the meaning of the name would indicate only a single act of supplanting, yet he says עֲקָבַנִי זֶה פַעֲמַיִם (he has supplanted me these two times), for if his name had been עֲקָבוֹת or עֹקְבוֹת it would have indicated a supplanting two times." "<b>Or</b> it may intend along this line: <b>הֲכִי קָרָא שְׁמוֹ יַעֲקֹב</b> — and he did not say עָקְבָה or עָקֵב, for then it would indicate only a single act of supplanting; but יַעֲקֹב indicates continuity and persistence, and therefore by now he has already [supplanted him] two times."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:01.181820315Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}